      "writtenOn": "2025-09-16T20:07:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "They are not truly needed. Their presence here reserves some keymap space for them, which isn\u0027t necessary, but is mostly a reminder that once we stop supporting a device in the future, it needs to stay in this list in the future because their index in the list affects their keymapping.\n\nI left a comment [elsewhere](https://review.calyxos.org/c/CalyxOS/vendor_calyx/+/41394/comment/95f78310_682c0db3/) before I moved things around. I\u0027ll copy it here.\n\n\u003e It doesn\u0027t *have* to be *all* devices that have ever been supported. It could simply be all devices that will be supported when CalyxOS maintenance returns. But then I just need to know what to call that.\n\u003e \n\u003e Based on the ID layout / reservations (see keymapper_yubihsm.sh), we have \"address space\" (ID space) for 223 devices, so it doesn\u0027t hurt much to have them all here right now.\n\nLooks like I was worried about the name \"all_devices\"? I think we could get away with calling it all_devices even if it doesn\u0027t include some of the earliest devices we supported.",
